      "message": "The original tree has\n\nprebuilts/sdk/Android.bp\nprebuilts/sdk/BUILD.bazel\n\nThis CL adds (an empty)\n\nprebuilts/sdk/BUILD \n\nSomehow the original BUILD.bazel didn\u0027t mark prebuilts/sdk as a subpackage, but the new BUILD file does\n\nThis seems to cause a number of build errors - e.g. bazel build //bionic/... fails with errors like\n\nERROR: /usr/local/google/home/ruperts/aosp-3/prebuilts/sdk/BUILD.bazel:3:14: Label \u0027//prebuilts/sdk:tools/linux/bin/aapt2\u0027 is invalid because \u0027prebuilts/sdk/tools\u0027 is a subpackage; perhaps you meant to put the colon here: \u0027//prebuilts/sdk/tools:linux/bin/aapt2\u0027?\n\nERROR: /usr/local/google/home/ruperts/aosp-3/prebuilts/sdk/BUILD.bazel:5:12: Label \u0027//prebuilts/sdk:tools/linux/bin/zipalign\u0027 is invalid because \u0027prebuilts/sdk/tools\u0027 is a subpackage; perhaps you meant to put the colon here: \u0027//prebuilts/sdk/tools:linux/bin/zipalign\u0027?\n\nI\u0027m still a little confused why the original BUILD.bazel didn\u0027t mark prebuilts/sdk as a subpackage. \n\nBut maybe we should not generate empty BUILD files if a BUILD.bazel file exists?\n\ncc ahumesky@",
